<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame frame--creed">
    <p class="kicker">8.6 &mdash; written by the author against himself</p>
    <h2 id="t-open">Two Open Challenges to a Complete Proof</h2>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Uniqueness of f(z).</strong> Proving that this particular meromorphic function is the
        only mathematically permissible one when algorithmic (Solomonoff) induction is lifted onto the
        complex plane. Until that is done, the function is a choice that happens to work.</li>
      <li><strong>A differential derivation of κ.</strong> Deriving κ = 1/4π² directly from a fundamental
        topological invariant &mdash; a Chern number or an Euler characteristic of a four-dimensional
        manifold undergoing Möbius inversion &mdash; so that no appearance of post-hoc tuning
        remains.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="muted">Both are stated in the Unified Edition itself. A framework that lists its own two
      unpaid debts in the same chapter as its headline result is doing something most cosmologies do
      not, and the site keeps that on the page rather than in a footnote.</p>
  </div>
</section>

